ry:**\n\n✅ **Line 1**: Single date with IPv4 → Matched `2026-01-01`\n✅ **Line 2**: Multiple dates with IPv4 → Matched `2026-01-03` (the **last** date, not the first)\n✅ **Line 3**: IPv4 but no date → No match\n✅ **Line 4**: Feb 29 (valid in all years) + multiple dates with IPv4 → Matched `2026-12-31` (the last date)\n✅ **Line 5**: Date but no IPv4 → No match (correctly requires IPv4)\n✅ **Line 6**: Invalid fake date `1134-12-1234` with IPv4 → No match (correctly rejected)\n✅ **Line 7**: Date with trailing text `-text` and IPv4 → Matched `2026-01-01` (word boundary prevents false match with the suffix)\n✅ **Line 8**: Invalid date `2026-04-31` (April has 30 days) with valid `2026-04-30` and IPv4 → Matched `2026-04-30` (invalid date skipped, last valid matched)\n\nThe regex correctly:\n- Matches only dates on lines containing an IPv4 address\n- Returns only the **last date** when multiple dates exist on a line\n- Validates month/day ranges (April can't have 31 days, February can have 29)\n- Rejects false matches like `1134-12-1234`\n- Uses word boundaries to avoid matching dates that are part of longer identifiers\n\nThe solution is ready at `/app/regex.txt`.","ttft_ms":96213,"type":"result","duration_ms":125096,"uuid":"44f639ba-8406-4588-abcf-6faece9b301d","ttft_stream_ms":791,"time_to_request_ms":85,"queued_turn_count":0}
